r's own caveat.\n  - claim: The cross-table copy control flipped 0 of 2 trials, \"which is consistent with the budgets not being artefacts of an already-reversed pair or of row position.\"\n  - evidence: claims_grounding.json claim \"Empty-set control flips no case; cross-table copy control flips 0 of 2 trials\" cites only final.evidence.episodes, which records copy_control {flips:0, trials:2} with no construction detail. paper.tex Method states \"we make no claim about them\". Supplement states \"its construction is not documented in the staged evidence\".\n  - requested_fix: Keep the empty-set interpretation only if wanted (empty set flipped no case). For the copy control, report only \"0 flips in 2 trials\" and delete the \"row position\" inference.\n- `verified-protocol-wording` (Introduction (Research question), Results Table tab:cases caption, Contributions): The paper repeatedly states that the evaluator source is not staged and that it could not inspect how the evaluator verifies a returned set. Calling the protocol or the budgets \"verified\" overstates the evidence. The only inspectable refit is the candidate's own.\n  - claim: Budgets are measured \"by one verified protocol\", and $k$ is \"the verified number of removed rows\".\n  - evidence: paper.tex Intro (\"we could not inspect how it verifies them\"), Method comparators section, Supplement \"Controls and qualification details\" (\"we could not inspect how the evaluator verifies it\"). claims_grounding.json: \"Evaluator source for comparators B1-B3 and the controls is not staged; only recorded outcomes ... are reported\".\n  - requested_fix: Replace \"verified\" with \"evaluator-recorded\". For example, \"one evaluator-recorded protocol\" and \"the recorded number of removed rows\".\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[0].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\n- figures[0].font_sizes.axis below minimum: 8.0 < 9.0\n- figures[1].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.5 < 10.0\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 2074 < 2400\n- figures[2].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.5 < 10.0\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1835 < 2400\n# Draft reference gap analysis\n\n**Status:** ready. Three targeted retrieval targets.\n\nCoverage of Bradley–Terry theory (extensions, existence/consistency, uncertainty) is dense. The existing bibliography does not cover three areas the draft relies on or motivates itself with. The draft concedes this in its \"Scope of the bibliography\" paragraph and in the Extended limitations. Numeric claims are grounded in `paper_data.json` and are not targets.\n\n## Missing literatures\n- Chatbot Arena / MT-Bench pairwise LLM evaluation and the datasets used\n- Influence functions and leave-one-out / Cook's-distance-style deletion diagnostics\n- Manipulation and rigging of crowd-vote or pairwise-comparison rankings\n\n## Targets\n\n1. **arena-leaderboard-context** (Introduction, high, benchmark_context)\n   - Anchor: \"Leaderboards that aggregate 'which of A and B is better' judgments into Bradley–Terry (BT) ratings are used to choose models…\"\n   - Reason: The motivating claim about leaderboard use has no citation. The Data section uses Arena 55k/140k and MT-Bench human judgments without citing the platform or dataset papers.\n   - Search topics: Chatbot Arena platform paper; MT-Bench human judgments / LLM-as-a-judge; Arena human-preference dataset.\n\n2. **influence-deletion-method** (Problem Setup and Method, high, background)\n   - Anchor: \"Deleting row $i$ perturbs the stationarity condition by $-\\nabla\\ell_i$, so a Newton step predicts the change of the gap…\"\n   - Reason: The first-order influence formula with leverage correction is the core of the studied configuration and the basis of the B2 comparator. It has no citation to influence-function or case-deletion literature. Only Broderick et al. is cited.\n   - Search topics: influence functions for black-box predictions; Cook's distance / case deletion in logistic regression; one-step leave-one-out approximations for M-estimators.\n\n3. **manipulation-positioning** (Related Work, medium, positioning)\n   - Anchor: \"Work on adversarial manipulation of crowd-vote leaderboards, on evaluation practices of arena-style platforms, and on influence functions…\"\n   - Reason: The draft motivates the removal budget through deliberate action and rigging, then disclaims any positioning against that work. One or two citations would replace the disclaimer.\n   - Search topics: adversarial vote manipulation of LLM arena leaderboards; robustness of pairwise-comparison rankings to corrupted comparisons.\n\n## Not targeted\nRelated-work paragraphs on BT extensions, estimation and uncertainty are well supported. Adding more there would only grow the bibliography.\npostdraft_citation_weave_agent_claude_20261111_075327.log\npostdraft_citation_weave_prompt.md\npostdraft_reference_query_plan.json\npostdraft_reference_query_plan.md\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_agent_claude_20261111_075327.log\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_prompt.md\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\npostdraft_reference_retrieval.log\npostdraft_references.bib\npostdraft_references_provenance.json\n46403 paper.tex\n22237 references.bib\n68640 total\n52","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
