{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvrDG4CpiC8516fwp5tR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the development-stage section, table, supplement, and downstream mentions of the unregistered sub-scores."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":74147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5d6d8e7-1586-4e3e-91a9-1b285ebf7cc5","uuid":"37293ff1-d828-497b-b818-b851d0486720","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:46:45.879Z","request_id":"req_011CgvrDFF6P5mvkw21Pq6zv"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvrDG4CpiC8516fwp5tR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KoMYWpPfsQz9NoXz6ATvhS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b,cnt=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==cnt,(s.count(a),a[:60])\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"On the development tables only aggregates are recorded: the studied configuration's aggregate score of 0.4993 equals the logged aggregate influence-only reference score of 0.4993 (Section~\\\\ref{sec:dev}), and no per-case development budgets are recorded.\",\"On the development tables only total scores are recorded (Section~\\\\ref{sec:dev}); no per-family, per-case or per-comparator development breakdown is recorded, so no development comparison with an influence-only reference is possible.\")\n# dev section\ni=s.index(\"\\\\subsection{Development tables: a three-way tie and an unflipped expert table}\")\nj=s.index(\"\\\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\")\nnew=r\"\"\"\\subsection{Development tables: a three-way tie}\\label{sec:dev}\nTable~\\ref{tab:dev} reports the development evaluation of three search configurations: the influence-guided configuration studied above (Configuration 1) and two further configurations that are identified in the evidence only by their titles, a cell-aggregated relaxed removal search (Configuration 2) and a stationarity-LP target-rating search (Configuration 3). All three scored 0.4993, the same as the starting baseline (difference 0.0); all three were scored (3 of 3, none missing). % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study]]\nThe registry records only these total scores and per-episode runtimes (about 1.3 s, 2.0 s and 114 s); no per-family, per-case or per-comparator development breakdown is recorded, so we report none and draw no conclusion about which development case or design drives the total. In particular, we make no statement about whether pairs in the six-model MT-Bench table flip within its cap of 68 rows. Their source is not part of the staged inspectable evidence for Configurations 2 and 3, so we make no statement about their algorithms beyond their titles; we mention them only because their total score did not exceed that of the starting baseline.\n\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Development evaluation (Arena 55k and MT-Bench human; seeds 11 and 12). Scores are not comparable with held-out scores, which use different tables. No per-family or per-case breakdown is recorded.}\n\\label{tab:dev}\n\\small\n\\begin{tabular}{lrr}\n\\toprule\nConfiguration & Total score & Time / episode (s)\\\\\n\\midrule\nConfiguration 1 (studied) & 0.4993 & 1.3\\\\\nConfiguration 2 & 0.4993 & 2.0\\\\\nConfiguration 3 & 0.4993 & 114\\\\\n\\midrule\nStarting baseline & 0.4993 & --\\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#all_programs]] scores and durations of the three configurations\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study]] baseline score\n\\end{table}\n\nNo expert-design result exists on held-out data, and the development stage cannot say whether the expert table is easier or harder to reverse than the crowd tables. The expert-judgment design is therefore unmeasured in this paper's evidence.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+new+s[j:]\nrep(\"(ii) \\\\emph{No claim about expert or model-judge designs on held-out data.} The only expert-design evidence is a six-model development table with no flip within the cap and an unknown cause; no model-judge data were evaluated.\",\"(ii) \\\\emph{No claim about expert or model-judge designs.} The six-model expert table appears only in the development stage, where only total scores are recorded; no expert design was measured on held-out data and no model-judge data were evaluated.\")\nrep(\"The expert-judgment development table did not flip within the cap, for an unknown reason. Natural\",\"The expert-judgment design was not measured on held-out data, and the development stage records only total scores, so we make no claim about it. Natural\")\n# supplement dev detail\ni=s.index(\"\\\\subsection{Development tables: additional detail}\")\nj=s.index(\"\\\\subsection{Algorithmic specification\")\ns=s[:i]+r\"\"\"\\subsection{Development tables: additional detail}\nThe evidence registry records, for each of the three development configurations, a total score (0.4993) and per-episode runtimes, and for the starting baseline a total score (0.4993). No sub-scores, flip rates, comparator references or control gaps are recorded for the development stage, so none are reported here. Search scores and held-out scores belong to different evaluation scopes and tables and should not be compared. All three development configurations were scored (3 of 3, 0 unscored), so there is no missing development evidence. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#all_programs]] total score only\n\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nrep(\"The development side adds one expert table of six participants.\",\"The development side adds one expert table of six participants, for which no breakdown is recorded.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"0\\.9987\\|0\\.0695\\|0\\.5007\\|0\\.3153\\|expert\" paper.tex | cut -c1-220"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":74147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5d6d8e7-1586-4e3e-91a9-1b285ebf7cc5","uuid":"60fb02a7-f749-4747-93c0-2b7f565d160e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:46:55.409Z","request_id":"req_011CgvrDFF6P5mvkw21Pq6zv"}
